      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "IIRC, there already is a \"hide all\" option for stickers. It's inside of the same menu that you'd use to place stickers.\n\nI did realize, though, that there isn't a toggle for that in the settings at all. It seems to only exists in the action (radial/circle) menu. Maybe that could change soon?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-09-29T08:57:30.110Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Hello Devs,\n\nI've noticed there's no option to globally hide all stickers, this raises the following problem: \n\nIf a group of trolls join a world and puts NSFW stickers everywhere, people shouldn’t have to find those users to block them to remove them. \n\nThey also shouldn't have to focus on each individual offending sticker to hide them.\n\nI'd recommend adding a ‘hide all’ function, because no-one should have to stare at something grotesque, open a menu, click a button, then check to see if it's gone and then repeat the process again and again.\n\nThank you :)",
